## Amplify env + IAM scripts (admin repo)

- Merge Bedrock keys **without wiping** other env: `scripts/set-amplify-bedrock-env.ps1`
  - Refuses update if `get-app` JSON is dirty (SSL noise) or existing key count &lt; 10.
- Full restore from dotenv: `scripts/set-amplify-env-vars.ps1` (replaces **all** app env — use carefully).
- IAM inline policy: `scripts/attach-amplify-bedrock-iam.ps1` + `documentation/admin_help_chat/bedrock-invoke-policy.json`
- Policy name: `AdminHelpBedrockInvoke` on role `AmplifySSRLoggingRole-1cc46167-ac65-414a-b580-7103432bd70a`.

```powershell
# Merge Bedrock onto prod hub (defaults), then the dev hub
.\scripts\set-amplify-bedrock-env.ps1
.\scripts\set-amplify-bedrock-env.ps1 -AppId d3qk5eouzr7b80
```

After env, `amplify.yml`, or compute-role changes: RELEASE `release/v1.0.0`. Add `--no-verify-ssl` when the AWS CLI fails with `CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED`. Never pass `--environment-variables` on `update-app` unless the JSON is the full map; that flag replaces every key.

## Short stub on the hubs, long answer locally

**Symptom:** localhost Admin Help writes a multi-step how-to. `https://www.adwiiseagent.ai/admin` and `https://dev.adwiiseagent.ai/admin` return one sentence such as `Admin Home: Returns to this dashboard so you can open another admin area. It does not edit tenant data.`

That sentence is `stubAdminHelpAnswer` in `src/lib/adminHelp/bedrock.ts`. `answerAdminHelpQuestion` uses the stub when Bedrock is off **or** `invokeAdminHelpBedrock` throws. `BEDROCK_ENABLED=true` on the Amplify app only means the route will try the call.

**Cause (2026-11-06):** both hubs already had `BEDROCK_ENABLED=true`, `BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1`, and `BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`. Inline policy `AdminHelpBedrockInvoke` was on the service role, but `computeRoleArn` was null. The Next.js server never assumed that role, so the SDK had no credentials and the catch block returned the knowledge-pack stub. Localhost works because the developer credential chain can call Bedrock.

**Fix both hubs** (`d3gov7yn1ctow1` prod, `d3qk5eouzr7b80` dev). The role ARN is `arn:aws:iam::224674645062:role/service-role/AmplifySSRLoggingRole-1cc46167-ac65-414a-b580-7103432bd70a`. Its trust policy must allow `amplify.amazonaws.com` to `sts:AssumeRole`.

1. Read `computeRoleArn` with `aws amplify get-app --app-id <id> --region us-east-2 --query app.computeRoleArn`.
2. Put `bedrock-invoke-policy.json` on that role as inline policy `AdminHelpBedrockInvoke` (`attach-amplify-bedrock-iam.ps1 -RoleName AmplifySSRLoggingRole-1cc46167-ac65-414a-b580-7103432bd70a`). The `us.` inference profile needs `bedrock:InvokeModel` and `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` on foundation models **and** inference profiles in `us-east-1`, `us-east-2`, and `us-west-2`. A us-east-1-only resource list denies the cross-region profile.
3. Set the compute role without touching env vars: `aws amplify update-app --app-id <id> --compute-role-arn <role-arn> --region us-east-2`. Confirm `length(keys(environmentVariables))` did not drop (prod 83, dev 85 after `ALL_TENANTS_ADMIN` was added).
4. RELEASE `release/v1.0.0`. A compute-role change is not live until the next release. Prod auto-build can be off, so start the job: `aws amplify start-job --app-id <id> --branch-name release/v1.0.0 --job-type RELEASE --region us-east-2`.
5. Sign in, ask Help, and check `POST /api/admin/help-chat`. `"backend":"bedrock"` is the live model. `"backend":"stub"` means invoke still failed; read CloudWatch `/aws/amplify/<appId>` for `[adminHelp] Bedrock invoke failed`.

Applied 2026-11-06: prod release **152** and dev release **15** succeeded with that compute role.

## Bolting Admin Help onto another frontend (satellite / clone)

1. Copy `src/lib/adminHelp/`, API route, `AdminHelpChat`, and mount in the admin layout client.
2. Add `@aws-sdk/client-bedrock-runtime`; set the three `BEDROCK_*` env vars.
3. Ensure Clerk-gated admin access before invoke.
4. Extend knowledge pack (`hubGuides`, `howTos`, `operatorGuides`, `routeMap`) for that product’s tiles — do not dump all `documentation/**/*.html` into the prompt.
5. Push Amplify env with the merge script (us-east-2 app id), attach `AdminHelpBedrockInvoke`, and set `computeRoleArn` to that role. A policy on the service role alone does not reach the Next.js server.
6. Keep retail Ask wired through Spring → engine if the clone has retail; do not merge the two chat APIs.

## Retail Ask (engine) — reminders

- Engine: `gas_station_ai_engine/llm/bedrock.py` — `explain` vs `ask`, account gate `PROJECT_ACCOUNT`.
- Amplify **cannot** reach the internal engine ALB; retail Ask stays Admin → Spring → `RETAIL_ENGINE_BASE_URL`.
- Admin Help must **not** reuse `/api/retail-brief/chat`.

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Admin Help → AI engine /v1/chat
❌ Browser → Bedrock with embedded AWS keys
❌ update-app with only BEDROCK_* after a failed get-app JSON parse (wipes env)
❌ Fine-tuning / “embed all admin pages into the model”
❌ Teaching SUPER_ADMIN-only flows to tenant ADMIN
❌ Treat BEDROCK_ENABLED=true as proof the live chat calls Bedrock
❌ Leave computeRoleArn null after attaching AdminHelpBedrockInvoke to the service role
❌ Limit the invoke policy to us-east-1 when the model id is a us. cross-region profile
```

```text
✅ Next.js server route + IAM role / default credential chain
✅ Curated knowledge pack + pathname retrieval
✅ Same Claude Sonnet model id, separate system prompt
✅ Amplify list/update in us-east-2; Bedrock invoke in us-east-1
✅ computeRoleArn set to the role that holds AdminHelpBedrockInvoke, then RELEASE
```

